Subject: A contracted layout can promise an int or a never-null object in any slot, the last one included

What this does
  - `js_aot_claim_ok` learns two promises: the tag is INT (`QJS_AOT_CLAIM_INT`) and an object of layout L that is never
    null or undefined (`QJS_AOT_CLAIM_OBJ_NN(L)`, 0x40 | L). The claim bytes are named constants; a layout id has six
    bits, so there are at most 63 layouts.
  - `js_aot_content_filled` checks every slot, the last included, and replaces `js_aot_content_enter` where the caller wrote
    every slot before the call (the five object-literal fills and the JSON build). `js_aot_content_last` checks the last
    slot after the caller wrote it, at the data-property adds (set, define, private define, global var define) and the two
    inline-cache adds that write the last slot after `js_aot_content_enter`.
  - Five overwrites of an existing slot reached no store hook: the main interpreter's inline-cache overwrite hit and its
    two own-property puts, and the two register interpreters' own-property puts. They call `js_aot_content_store` now.
  - Under `QJS_KIT_TEST_KNOBS` (set by the kit build only) the environment variable `QJS_AOT_NOCLAIMHOOK` turns the claim
    hooks off, for the kit's negative controls. The prototype test of the enter hook stays on.

Why we need it
  A compiled load can drop the tag test of an int field and the shape test of an object field only if every store into
  that slot keeps the promise. The last slot of a layout is written after the object adopts its shape, so the enter hook
  could not see it; the last slots of the benchmark's objects hold most of the tag tests. A store that breaks a promise
  sets the layout's bit of `aot_layout_broken`, the same one-way model as a prototype entering the layout.

  Soundness of the add paths: nothing runs JS between `add_property` returning and the write of the value at the hooked
  sites, so compiled code never sees the last slot unchecked. The other `add_property` callers pass flags no layout shape
  has (var-ref, accessor, auto-init, length, brand, array index), and the flags are part of the shape hash. The audit
  script requires every `add_property(` site to be followed by the hook or to carry such flags, and every slot write to be
  hooked within a few lines, with no function-wide allowlist entry for the interpreters.

  Behaviour is unchanged until the unit sets a claim.

Functions touched
  `js_aot_claim_ok`, `js_aot_content_enter_slow`, `js_aot_content_filled`, `js_aot_content_last`, `js_aot_content_store_slow`,
  `JS_SetPropertyInternal2`, `JS_DefineProperty`, `JS_CreateProperty`, `JS_DefineGlobalVar`, `JS_DefinePrivateField`,
  `regvm_put_field_add_hit`, `JS_CallInternal`, `js_regvm_execute`, `regvm_exec_one`, `js_cold_object_fill`,
  `regvm_t_object_fill`, `qjs_aot_object_fill_b`, `json_obj_adopt_shape`.

No.

